; t34_collfor.n — v16.1 `for` over ordered collections: the count slot takes
; an int (index loop, as before), a numeric string (coerced count), or a
; list / typed array / tensor (ELEMENT loop; length captured at entry —
; growth inside the loop does not extend the run). Dicts die (contained).
; Run: nk comp/tests/t34_collfor.n

0 t!
0 t2!
0 u!

; 1. list elements
[10 20 30] addeach for
t 60 eq check

; 2. plain count loop unchanged (index pushed)
5 cntf for
t2 100 eq check

; 3. typed-array elements
[1 2 3] int array dblf for
t2 112 eq check

; 4. empty collection: zero iterations
[] zerof for
t2 112 eq check

; 5. numeric string coerces to a count (not a char loop)
"3" strcf for
t2 142 eq check

; 6. string elements flow like any other element
list s6!
["a" "b"] upf for
s6 to_json "[\"a\",\"b\"]" eq check

; 7. break out of a collection loop
[1 2 3 4 5] brkf for
u 6 eq check

; 8. dict is not an ordered collection — dies (contained by try)
dict d2!
: d2 zerof for ret try ok# _#
ok 0 eq check

"coll-for-ok" print
ret

addeach: v! t v add t! ret 0
cntf: i! t2 i 10 mul add t2! ret 0
dblf: v! t2 v 2 mul add t2! ret 0
zerof: v! "bad" print ret 0
strcf: i! t2 i 10 mul add t2! ret 0
upf: v! s6 v append s6! ret 0
brkf: v!
  u v add u!
  u 6 eq bstop if
  ret 0
bstop: break
  ret 0
